**Theorem 6.3 (totality and all-size soundness).** $V_{\rm swap}$ is
total computable. Acceptance implies, simultaneously for every $n$ and
every original owned-seed network of prescribed incidence at most $L$,

$$
Z(\mathcal N;\mu,\ldots,\mu)\le C^n,
\qquad \beta_{d,L}(\mu)\le C.
\tag{OOA.24}
$$

Proof. Each enumeration and every rational power or comparison in the
definition is finite. If a network has positive mass, all its vertex
types have nonempty support-aware relations, by COK coverage. Its actual
radius-two patterns therefore require swap witnesses at every high
vertex. The rational majorants imply (OOA.16) uniformly over all full
contexts. The kernel arrays are assigned using each vertex's complete
actual decoration, and (OOA.21) gives its local domination. Corollary
5.2 bounds its mass by

$$
c_0^{n-t}\left[c_1(1-\delta/\Delta)^{1/(2B)}\right]^t\le C^n
$$

using (OOA.23). Zero mass is immediate; in particular an empty local
relation permits no positive global assignment. Taking the supremum
over all lengths gives (OOA.24). $\square$

